# Scenes staged from the skill's examples/ at build time by scripts/stage-films.sh.
# Tracked once, as plugin/skills/mitate/examples/ — not twice. A pattern rather
# than a list, so a sixth example needs no edit here.
#
# EVERYTHING in films/ is ignored, not just *.html. The narrower `films/*.html`
# would have let a staged .json, sprite sheet or map file get tracked by
# accident, which is the second-copy problem arriving through a side door.
#
# .gitkeep is the one exception and exists so the DIRECTORY survives a clone.
# Git stores no empty directories, so with nothing tracked here a fresh checkout
# had no site/films/ at all — which is how both brackets died with ENOENT the
# first time they ran anywhere but a laptop that had already built.
films/*
!films/.gitkeep

# NO film is ever tracked here, as of 0.16.35. gearbox-neon.html was the one
# negated file — a showcase-only neon variant — and was untracked on the owner's
# call: it was 66% of the site's tracked bytes for a variant the site does not
# need. It is GENERATED by stage-films.sh from gearbox.html plus the neon bible,
# which is what bibles.md claims is possible, executed rather than asserted.
